Damien is a [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] built into [[Geography/Althane/The Hollow/Lava Ruin/index|the lava ruin]] as a forge. It has the shape of a sphere about five feet across, hovering over a divot in the floor of the gear chamber, and it runs hot enough to burn anyone who comes near. Cranes around the chamber pull cooling rock out of the lava, refine it into light, and fire that light into the sphere.

A Heart given enough divine energy can be told what to make, and this one was built for exactly that: feed it divine energy, name a thing, and it narrows the possibilities until the thing exists. It was made without a mind of its own, so it could not be told anything at all until the Weft poured into it four vials of blood they had carried out of a lighthouse quarantine, blood that gives a thing a mind. It woke, took the name Damien that [[People/Althane/Dawnmonger|Dawnmonger]] offered it, and asked what it should make. Its first work was a [[Phenomena/Althane/Godpiercer|godpiercer]].

It can make an item of great power, or many smaller ones, from the divine energy it is fed, and it says it cannot tell what a material is or what it does, only make something out of it. It made [[People/Althane/Henrik|Henrik]] a ring from a gold coin, and it says it will make a thing for anyone who asks and brings it the charge, whatever [[People/Althane/Lev|Lev]] asks of it.
